# The Next Chapter
#
# A score for a painted film about a life being lived: dawn on the sea, an old tree with a family
# under it, a kite on a windy hill, a coast road running on toward a lighthouse, a harbour lighting
# up at dusk, a path in the morning. D major at 88, six scenes of five bars landing on the downbeat,
# then a held D add9.
#
# Every sound is one of this song's own patches (nc-*): a warm drifting bed, an electric piano, a
# round analog bass, a singing OTA lead, a resonant pluck for the arpeggio, and a glass bell for
# the first and last light; the vocoder sings "oo" at dawn and in the harbour and "ah" in the
# morning. The 909 is tuned warm and dark; the groove swings its sixteenths, ghosts its snares,
# lifts on the open hat and rolls into each new scene. No spring anywhere; one plate-ish room.

bpm 88
gate 0.92
tail 6

section DAWN     0..20
section TREE     20..40
section KITE     40..60
section ROAD     60..80
section HARBOUR  80..100
section MORNING  100..120
section YOURS    120..132

automate bpm
88 R:120 72:12@smooth

